data: {"type":"agent_chunk","agent":"analyst","content":"- **Core mechanism:** A Cas9 nuclease guided by synthetic RNA cuts DNA at a chosen site [1], creating double-strand breaks [3].\n- **Targeted editing:** Because cuts are site-specific, edits can insert, delete, modify, or replace DNA at defined locations rather than randomly [3].\n- **Claims outpace evidence:** Broad disease-treatment claims come from a news headline [4], and HIV elimination comes from a conference-style headline reporting cell-culture results [5]. Neither shows clinical efficacy."}

